There are indeed a couple other choices to enter the Castle. Using the
drawbridge, though, is very a simple means to smash all monsters by the
guillotine principle (which certainly can be considered to be an exploit;
cf. bug C343-318). This option is especially interesting for those liches
and disenchanters, and even for the eels in the moat if you like.

OTOH, it was never apparent to me why the separate "play the right tune"
disclosure while praying would be of any use; first it's rare to get - why
not just provide the second, i.e. the full disclosure "here's the tune"
message. IMO, the first message is something for the Oracle chit-chat and
fortune cookie's contents than a divine present. And the second message is
as well not really worth the effort; after all you can always play the game
of Mastermind to open the drawbridge. The larger "problem" is to get an
appropriate music instrument (especially if there were no barracks in your
game). I think that a more appropriate gift from your god would be a music
instrument (even one of the magic ones, if only to increase their appearance
frequency to some noticable degree) instead of the plain tune.

